SCHEDULE A -- EXCLUDED RECIPIENTS, TERRITORIES AND PURPOSES

A.1. Enumerated Authorities and Restricted Territories.

For this License, each authority or organisation below is an "Enumerated
Authority". A "Restricted Territory" is any territory in which an Enumerated
Authority exercises effective governmental authority, de jure or de facto:

  (a) the government of the People's Republic of China, the Democratic
      People's Republic of Korea, the Russian Federation, the Republic of
      Belarus, the Islamic Republic of Iran, the Republic of Cuba or the
      Republic of Azerbaijan;

  (b) the military authorities of Myanmar (Burma), including the Myanmar
      Armed Forces (Tatmadaw), the State Administration Council, the State
      Security and Peace Commission, and any military-appointed,
      military-controlled or successor governmental administration;

  (c) the Taliban, including the authorities operating as the "Islamic
      Emirate of Afghanistan"; Hamas (Harakat al-Muqawama al-Islamiyya),
      including the Izz al-Din al-Qassam Brigades; Islamic State, including
      ISIS, ISIL and Da'esh; Al-Qaeda (Al-Qaida); Sudan's Rapid Support
      Forces (RSF); or the Houthis (Ansar Allah), including their Supreme
      Political Council;

  (d) the de facto authorities operating as the "Pridnestrovian Moldavian
      Republic" (Transnistria), the "Republic of Abkhazia", the "Republic
      of South Ossetia" or "State of Alania", the "Donetsk People's
      Republic" or the "Luhansk People's Republic"; or Russian-installed
      occupation administrations in Crimea, Sevastopol, Donetsk, Luhansk,
      Kherson or Zaporizhzhia.

Naming an authority identifies an excluded recipient; it does not recognise
a claim to sovereignty, statehood or territorial title. The territorial
condition is limited to territories governed by the authorities specified
in A.1. The separate organisational conditions below apply wherever the
organisation or recipient operates.

A.2. Excluded Controlling Organisations.

A "Restricted Controlling Organisation" includes any political party,
movement, military organisation, security apparatus, council, collective
governing body or other organisation that directly or indirectly exercises
decisive political, military, security or financial control over an
Enumerated Authority, whether or not it holds formal governmental office
or is legally separate from that authority.

The following are also expressly excluded organisations, independently of
whether a relationship to an Enumerated Authority needs to be established:

  (a) the Chinese Communist Party (CCP), also called the Communist Party of
      China or CPC;
  (b) the Workers' Party of Korea;
  (c) the Communist Party of Cuba;
  (d) United Russia;
  (e) the New Azerbaijan Party (Yeni Azərbaycan Partiyası / YAP);
  (f) the Office of the Supreme Leader of Iran and the Islamic
      Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC);
  (g) the Presidential Administrations and Security Councils of Russia
      and Belarus, and the Presidential Administration of Azerbaijan;
  (h) the Myanmar military organisations and councils identified in A.1.

A.3. Related Bodies, Controlled Entities and Representatives.

The exclusions extend to any organ, agency, instrumentality, armed force,
security or intelligence service, political bureau, committee, regional
branch, military wing, state-owned or state-controlled entity, or other
entity owned or controlled, directly or indirectly, by a recipient described
in A.1, A.2 or A.4; and any person or entity acting for such a recipient.
For this Schedule, control includes the practical power, whether through
ownership, appointment, contract, financing or otherwise, to direct an
entity's management, policy, operations or relevant use of the Work.

Aliases, renamed bodies, successors, fronts and organisations operating
under the direction or control of an excluded recipient are included.
Legal separation, incorporation elsewhere, an intermediary, contractor,
nominee or proxy does not remove the exclusion.

A.4. Excluded Political Programmes and Organised Support.

A "Restricted Political Organisation" is any political party, movement,
association, network or other person or organisation whose official
programme, authoritative public statements or organised activities seek to
establish, preserve, restore, justify or materially extend an institutional
arrangement in which:

  (a) effective supreme governmental power is vested in an individual,
      party, military, religious establishment or other body without
      periodic, genuine, competitive elections and a practicable means
      of peaceful replacement through pluralistic political participation;
      or
  (b) meaningful political competition or peaceful replacement of those
      exercising governmental power is prevented by the systematic
      suppression of opposition, independent adjudication, freedom of
      expression, association or peaceful assembly.

This definition also includes a person or organisation that knowingly
provides material financial, operational, technical or organised
promotional support to maintain, impose or expand such an arrangement,
whether or not it currently holds governmental office or is established in
a Restricted Territory. It includes organised support for a recipient
identified in A.1 or A.2 when that support materially advances such a
recipient's political programme, governing apparatus or capacity.

A.5. Material Benefit and Restricted Recipients.

A "Restricted Recipient" means an authority, organisation, body, person or
entity within A.1, A.2, A.3 or A.4.

"Material Benefit" means an identifiable economic, operational, military,
security, surveillance, censorship, coercive, organisational, political or
propagandistic advantage to a Restricted Recipient that is more than merely
speculative or incidental to unrelated lawful activity. It includes
product or service development, technical integration, revenue generation,
expense avoidance, training or improving systems, expanding operational
capacity, recruitment, fundraising, political mobilisation and organised
promotional or legitimising activity, whether obtained directly or through
another person or entity.

Historical study, quotation, criticism, independent journalism, legal
representation and documentation of abuses do not, by their subject matter
alone, constitute organised support or Material Benefit. This clarification
does not authorise access by an otherwise Restricted Recipient, a supply to
such a recipient, a use for that recipient's actual Material Benefit, or an
Exercise of Rights from a Restricted Territory.

A recipient's place of birth, ancestry, ethnicity, religion or nationality
alone does not establish organisational status under A.2 through A.4.
The express territorial condition in Section 10(c)(i) is unaffected.

A.6. Provenance.

The enumerated territorial, organisational, control and intermediary
conditions in A.1 through A.3 are adapted from the non-license Terms of Use
published at https://10671435.xyz/#help-terms, as retrieved on
14 November 2026. Version 1.1 additionally enumerates the government of
the People's Republic of China in A.1(a), so that the territorial condition
applies wherever that government exercises effective governmental authority,
de jure or de facto. This is an express amendment to the enumerated list,
rather than a claim that version 1.0 already contained that restriction.
In this project these conditions operate as express conditions of
the copyright and patent permissions, together with Section 10 and the
additional definitions in this Schedule. The website's separate source-code
license and third-party data licenses do not govern this project's own code.

